# Who reviews what. One owner per graded component, because the viva is
# individual: each owner defends their own package, so a change inside someone
# else's package is a change they cannot defend.
#
# NOTE ON ENFORCEMENT: this file currently only auto-requests reviewers. `main`
# has no branch protection and no ruleset, so a CODEOWNERS review is requested
# and not required, and a direct push to `main` bypasses it entirely. Making it
# binding is one ruleset -- "require a pull request" plus "require review from
# Code Owners" -- and that is a deliberate decision, not an oversight.
#
# Last line wins in CODEOWNERS, so the fallback is first and the specific
# paths come after.

# Fallback: the repository owner, for anything not claimed below.
*                                   @learntocode2013

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P1 — domain, knowledge & memory
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/oncall-knowledge/         @learntocode2013
/packages/oncall-memory/            @learntocode2013
/data/                              @learntocode2013
/docs/memory-policy.md              @learntocode2013
/docs/severity-policy.md            @learntocode2013
/artifacts/retrieval/               @learntocode2013

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P2 — orchestration, planning & improvement
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/oncall-graph/             @morevk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P3 — tools, human control & guardrails
#
# Includes the pre-tool hook and the MCP servers.
#
# NOMINAL OWNER: @rajabharathi29, who is not available. Reviews route to
# @learntocode2013 instead, which is the same covering arrangement ADR-0004
# already records -- P1 wrote that record while covering for P3, and it states
# that P3 owns the code regardless of who writes it.
#
# @rajabharathi29 is deliberately NOT listed as a second owner here: GitHub
# requests review from EVERY owner on a line, so naming an unavailable person
# would park a pending review request on every tools PR and make the file look
# like it is routing work that nobody is doing. Add them back when they return.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/oncall-tools/             @learntocode2013

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P4 — evaluation & red team
#
# oncall-lab holds the fault manifest's root cause, so it sits behind the
# oracle boundary with the rest of evaluation (ADR-0004 notes P4/P5 own it).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/oncall-eval/              @ravishankarkumar
/packages/oncall-lab/               @ravishankarkumar
/eval/                              @ravishankarkumar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P5 — deployment & observability
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/oncall-service/           @ravishankarkumar
/deploy/                            @ravishankarkumar
/.github/                           @ravishankarkumar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared surfaces
#
# oncall-contracts is imported by every package and imports nothing, so a
# change here reaches all five components. Two reviewers on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/oncall-contracts/         @learntocode2013 @morevk
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @learntocode2013 @morevk
/docs/decisions/                    @learntocode2013 @morevk
